  "notes": {
    "checker-verdict": "Decides how serious each verdict of the formal checker is.",
    "checker-verdict.calcs.verdict": "A verdict: what was checked (a property, that a value read is defined, that a component is called within its requires, that an event can happen, or something the checker could not express at all) and how it came out. Something skipped, or out of range, is a warning (out-of-range). An event no trace reaches is a warning (unreached-case); one that is reached says nothing. A broken property, a value read where it is not defined, and a call outside the callee's requires are errors (property, undefined-value, requires-broken); anything that holds says nothing."
  },
